":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjhcorporate","html_url":"https://github.com/mjhcorporate","followers_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjhcorporate/followers","following_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjhcorporate/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjhcorporate/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjhcorporate/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjhcorporate/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjhcorporate/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjhcorporate/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjhcorporate/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/mjhcorporate/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2024-07-01T15:36:15Z","updated_at":"2024-07-01T15:36:15Z","body":"Not a template I am missing, but a bug in a current template. I ask for a nodeJS/express REST service like this:\r\n<img width=\"474\" alt=\"image\" src=\"https://github.com/microsoft/vscode-copilot-release/assets/49681105/4a1d8e01-b00b-4e37-8106-a535e01d96ca\">\r\nThe result is JavaScript classes that use `static` methods. This is unusual. But what is worse, in most cases, the class with static methods is instantiated as something like `const controller = new Controller()`, which breaks the static methods. (In JS, static methods are not available on the instances, only on the class!)\r\nIs there a way to see which templates are used for inspiration? Is there a way to change these templates?","author_association":"NONE","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/vscode-copilot-release/issues/comments/2200478216/reactions","total_count":0,"+1":0,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/microsoft/vscode-copilot-release/issues/commen